    {
      "_id": "626d2d24ad8ca509",
      "name": "Training Reference: Runecraft Grammar",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>What Quill Teaches Stellan</h2>\n<p>Quill reinforces the exact structure already present in Stellan's Runecrafting feature.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A complete inscription is a sentence: <strong>subject, Root Rune or Runes, scope, trigger, and anchor</strong>.</li>\n<li>Knowing a rune's name does not mean Stellan knows its glyph. He must discover and study the graphic form before using it as a known Root Rune.</li>\n<li>At level 4, Stellan can already Countermark and compose temporary two-rune sentences using known Root Runes.</li>\n<li>Quill teaches him to diagnose why a sentence works, which part can be opposed, and which edits would change the effect without pretending every ward is simply an “off switch.”</li>\n<li>Quill grants no extra Rune Charges.</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote><p>Most apprentices learn nouns and immediately attempt murder. Grammar is what keeps the building standing.</p></blockquote>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide — Ossuary Exchange Vendors",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
