    {
      "_id": "2e7aa98acd482a24",
      "name": "Side Quest: The Extremely Specific Door",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>The Extremely Specific Door</h2>\n<p>An old warehouse door refuses every recognized worker. Quill has been hired to repair it and has decided delegation is a sign of leadership.</p>\n<blockquote><p>It's old municipal runework. Dangerous? Worse. Amended.</p></blockquote>\n<p>The original inscription allowed authorized custodians to enter. Centuries of owners added exceptions, definitions, and countermarks until the sentence now recognizes one particular dead rat as the only valid custodian.</p>\n<p>Stellan can solve the problem by tracking down the rat's remains and proving the absurd condition, or by correctly reading and Countermarking the inscription within his existing mechanics.</p>\n<p><strong>Reward:</strong> Quill may teach Stellan the graphic form of <strong>one Tier I Root Rune chosen by the GM</strong> that Stellan does not already know. Stellan must study the glyph; this counts as discovering and studying it under the existing Runecrafting rule. No extra charges are granted.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide — Ossuary Exchange Vendors",
          "book": "",
