    {
      "name": "Lore Reference: Cladis's Trail",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Cladis's Trail (GM only)</h2><p>Quill has collected Cladis's trail marks for years: the bold <strong>Threshold-family wayfinding marks</strong> (\"a road that is also a door\", like the CLADIS marks on Europa's father's map), the <strong>open claim</strong> in the custody ledger, and an <strong>outstanding tag</strong>.</p><p><strong>Quill's aim (SETTLED):</strong> bring Cladis back so she can enlist the Rhime Goddess, who needs her name carried back into the Wyrd to fight the Niorghast and stop him resurrecting Nior. Quill knows the name from the trail but will not say it aloud; the Goddess writes it on the Stolen Shard in Scene 7.</p><h3>Sample lines</h3><ul><li>[EARN] \"She left marks for whoever came after. A trail. Your map is one. We follow it.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"There is a name. It isn't ours to say in a tavern.\"</li><li>[EARN] \"A thread tied in the wrong place can be tied again. Two knots and a good line. That's all.\"</li><li><em>(On the anchor's Hunger trace)</em> \"Hunger. Her name has that word in it. I don't like that either.\"</li></ul>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
